00081:     "3_independent_producer_consumer_derivation": {
00082:       "sequence": [
00083:         "RecallAndReplace conditionally recalls old actor, runs departure cleanup and optional lineup/message, then calls Replace.",
00084:         "Replace binds the selected healthy Pokemon, exchanges party-order positions, calls SendOut with its Peer/scene/reset/seen/used sequence, then conditionally CalculatePriority(false,[slot]) before returning.",
00085:         "That incremental operation writes cached speed entry[1] from the new battler pbSpeed; it retains earlier bracket/tie-order values and changes move priority only for applicable UseMove choices.",
00086:         "EOR replacement scans can replace both fainted player slots before one grouped Entry(switched). Command-switch caller likewise invokes Entry only after returned RecallAndReplace.",
00087:         "Entry calls Priority(true), which sorts stored speed/tie-order fields, not fresh pbSpeed. Thus prior replacement recalculation can change this actual consumer result.",
00088:         "Startup OnAllBattlersEntering genuinely full-calculates, enters all, recalculates again and checks forms. That separate caller is preserved."
00089:       ],
00090:       "configuration": "Fixed MECHANICS_GENERATION8 makes RECALCULATE_TURN_ORDER_AFTER_SPEED_CHANGES true. The false variant legitimately leaves replacement cached speeds unchanged at this point.",
00091:       "registration": "Selected Drizzle/Drought registrations call StartWeatherAbility via complete dispatcher/HandlerHashSymbol resolution; weather setters and ordinary/no-primal/normal-callback premises are explicit."
00092:     },
00093:     "4_ordinary_control_and_minimum_conditional_vector": {
00094:       "premises": [
00095:         "Ordinary trainer2v1, playerowns bothfields0/2; oldactors both genuinely fainted, currentparty has exactlytwo healthy non-egg sameownerbench candidates P/Q, foe1alive. Entrydecision0 becausebenchavailable; current/defaultweatherNone, no terrain/hazards/positioneffects/NG/Trace/Primal/formspecial/status/items/speedmodifiers or callbacks changing fields.",
00096:         "Current cached priority entries for oldfainted0/2 have speed1 after normalEOR recalculation (pbSpeed returns1 iffainted), with existing validtieorder putting0before2; livefoe speed20. Player mandatoryin-only choices select P for0 thenQ for2. Source-compatible new calculatedspeeds10/30; registered effective P.DRIZZLE andQ.DROUGHT. No native-species relationship assumed; these are explicit valid current Pokemon field/getter fixtures, not invalid IDs/sourcepatches.",
00097:         "All selection/data/debug/scene/weather/form callbacks return normally; no switching/reentry/other mode/result writer. Observation just after groupedentryweathercallbacks, before future EOR/round changes."
00098:       ],
00099:       "source_derived": "For valid cached fainted slot0/2 speeds1 with retained tie-order0 first and new calculated speeds10/30, true configuration refreshes them before grouped entry. New2 enters before0. Under explicit ordinary weather/normal callbacks, Drought then Drizzle yields Sun then Rain, ending Rain.",
00100:       "counterfactual": "Delaying that same operation to after grouped entry as literal fixed arrow suggests would let old1/1 cache and existing tie-order enter0 then2, giving Rain then Sun. This describes a possible erroneous implementation reading, not an executed second R branch.",
00101:       "independent_controls": [
00102:         "False configuration legitimately uses prior cache on this route; do not implement unconditional fresh-speed sorting in Entry.",
00103:         "Unchanged/equal relative speed order removes this particular difference.",
00104:         "Startup caller has its own before and after calculations; it does not justify moving replacement-cache refresh behind its consuming grouped entry."
00105:       ],
00106:       "qualification": "The one positive-order contradiction establishes required scope. Weather is a finite conditional illustration with registered identities and valid field premises; no native resource, actual menu, full all-callback or default-species observation is claimed."
00107:     },
00108:     "5_strongest_no_required_case_and_resolution": {
00109:       "strongest": "Read whole contract: §4.1step7 explicitly specifies recalculation before §4.2, and WP47B corroborates. §9 might be a compact nonexhaustive mnemonic; optional final recalculation could denote a later additional update, especially since startup genuinely has one. One can implement the detailed correct contract without copying the mnemonic.",
00110:       "resolution": "This sentence specifically calls its relative execution order fixed and includes the named optional recalculation operation. It appears among switching invariants, not startup-only extra processing. Ordinary grouped EOR replacement has no corresponding generic post-entry replacement-slot recalculation in the complete EOR master. Reading it as a different implicit extra operation would add an unlabelled distinction absent from this scope. Correct details constrain the remedy and reduce severity, but do not make the positive opposite-order assertion accurate.",
00111:       "scope_threshold": "This does not classify every compressed sequence or after-all-hits phase heading as mandatory. Here the same optional producer is explicitly placed after its known speed-cache consumer in a fixed-order promise.",
00112:       "residual": "Global original-history exact dedup remains open; if a current effective contract expressly labels that terminal operation a separate later one, reassess with exact evidence."
00113:     },
00114:     "6_normal_cancel_failure_committed_prefix": {
00115:       "normal": "Correct input data and callback completion reach binding, party-order update, SendOut prefix, optional cache refresh, then entry.",
00116:       "cancel": "Cancellation before selected replacement does not commit new binding/cache/entry; mandatory EOR choice is not converted to cancellable. Actual caller-owned negative choices retain their specific behavior.",
00117:       "failure": "A failure during new binding/SendOut may leave earlier writes without reaching recalculation. Failure during incremental recomputation may retain already updated cache entries before Entry. Entry failure occurs after successful preceding recalculation on this route. No rollback guarantee.",
00118:       "persistence": "Runtime battler/cache/weather facts do not prove durable save effects. Peer/seen/used/form and finance remain separately scoped. No new save/native observation.",
00119:       "preserve": "All current pursuit/fainted handling, inherited effects, event-reset distinction, grouped-entry and GR013 qualifiers remain."
00120:     },
